<title>FRANCE: Juppe hopes lira ERM entry prelude to euro entry.</title>
<headline>Juppe hopes lira ERM entry prelude to euro entry.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Alain Juppe said on Wednesday he hoped the decision last weekend to bring the Italian lira back into the European Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) was a prelude to Italy joining the single currency.</p>
<p>&quot;The return of the Italian lira into the EMS, which is I hope a prelude to the Italian currency's entry into the European currency, is from this point of view good news for France and good news for French companies, especially those in sectors such as textiles which were destabilised by the competitive devaluation of the lira,&quot; he said in a parliamentary debate on Europe.</p>
</text>
